    "136": [
        "The problem of solving the Sokoban puzzle, where the player pushes boxes to target locations in a warehouse, is known to be NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Rush Hour sliding block puzzle, where the goal is to move a specific car out of a congested parking lot, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Lights Out puzzle, where toggling lights affects neighboring lights with the goal of turning all lights off, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Nonograms, also known as Picross or Griddlers, which involves filling in cells based on numerical clues to reveal a hidden picture, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Tetris packing problem, which involves fitting a set of Tetris pieces into a container without overlaps, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Peg Solitaire puzzle, where the goal is to eliminate pegs by jumping over them to reach a single peg in a specific position, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Sliding Puzzle, such as the 15 puzzle, where tiles are moved within a frame to reach a target configuration, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Block Puzzle, where blocks must be moved or rotated to fit into a specific shape or space, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Pipe Puzzle, involving connecting pipes to allow flow from a start to an end point, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Kakuro puzzle, which involves filling in cells with numbers to satisfy sum constraints, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Sudoku puzzle, where digits must be placed in a grid to satisfy row, column, and region constraints, is NP-complete",
        "The problem of solving the Minesweeper puzzle, where the goal is to identify all mines based on numerical clues, is NP-complete"
    ],
